 "script": "Elon Musk's XAI must face a pollution lawsuit, a judge ruled. A federal court in Mississippi ruled Friday, TechCrunch and Earthjustice report. The NAACP says XAI ran dozens of gas turbines without permits. They power its Colossus 2 data center near Memphis. XAI said the turbines were mobile, so exempt. The judge disagreed. Here's what it means beyond Memphis. XAI is building a one point two gigawatt gas plant for its AI. So the case goes ahead, and a bid to halt the turbines is still pending. Where should AI data centers get their power? Tell us below.",
